  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\hat{a}$ and $\\hat{b}$ be two unit vectors. If the vectors $\\vec{c}=\\hat{a}+2 \\hat{b}$ and $\\vec{d}=5 \\hat{a}-4 \\hat{b}$ are perpendicular to each other, then the angle between $\\hat{\\mathrm{a}}$ and $\\hat{\\mathrm{b}}$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "HRNP1",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi}{6}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "pLBMZ",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Yb5vU",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi}{3}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "FO2Hn",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi}{4}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{c}} \\cdot \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{d}}=\\overrightarrow{0} \\quad \\Rightarrow 5|\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{a}}|^2+6 \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{a}} \\cdot \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{b}}-8|\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{b}}|^2=0$\n$\\Rightarrow 6 \\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b}=3 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b}=\\frac{1}{2} \\quad \\Rightarrow(\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b})=\\frac{\\pi}{3}$",
    "image": null
  },
